ary if we no longer rely on it for visibility?"]],0,31],[7170530,20412,59,1.341,1.058,[[0,17]],[["4e780977_052a7ec1",46,0,1,"Same nit question."],["ddbdbb8c_c95e9289",47,0,0,"Nit: Does the following work instead of the setup method? ```suggestion base::test::ScopedFeatureList feature_list_{autofill::features::kYourSavedInfoSettingsPage}; ```"]],0,32],[7157891,20413,171,4.21,3.407,[[4,0.263,18,45],[3,0.237,12,44],[0,0.175,18,31],[16,0.098,0,16],[12,0.098,1,18],[17,0.067,0,9],[18,0.041,1,6],[19,0.01,0,1],[2,0.01,7,1]],[["09d04c8d_8bb8ff78",48,-3,1,"I think it should be added here too?"],["3fbf6f6c_2377f413",49,-3,1,"I'm unsure here whether it would not be better to list the entire enum and add a linter, usually this is recommended, but the access point enum is really large. However, it might come up that we need…"],["63dbb8bd_dfc30899",26,-3,1,"I think it's better to use constants than numbers for enums, see https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:chrome/browser/resources/settings/privacy_page/personalization_options.html#:~…"],["be118989_c8baf65d",50,-3,1,"suggestion: `Your saved info page in settings`"],["fd6a2639_c2c279f4",48,-3,1,"Same here"],["0926cab8_6f91a01e",51,-2,1,"style: `kSettings`"],["7d3fa025_b3757721",13,-2,1,"nit: I think it was good that you had the access point explicitly mentioned here, fits the other access point's histograms and makes it easier to search"],["dd95e7b3_a30c1e3f",51,-1,1,"It's better to use `LINT.ChangeIf()` guards for this. https://www.chromium.org/chromium-os/developer-library/guides/development/keep-files-in-sync/"]],0,33],[7185064,20416,185,4.21,3.407,[[4,0.256,19,47],[3,0.251,13,50],[0,0.161,19,31],[17,0.095,1,15],[16,0.09,1,16],[12,0.09,2,18],[18,0.038,2,6],[19,0.009,1,1],[2,0.009,8,1]],[["2cfed33f_49a64b89",52,0,1,"nit: could you please wrap this string at 80 columns? `git cl format` might do that automatically for you but if now, please insert an extra line break manually ```suggestion…"],["9518014c_fe71384c